    "introduction": "LondonMetric Property owns commercial real estate let to occupiers under leases intended to provide recurring rental income. Its portfolio includes logistics buildings and properties used for activities such as healthcare, convenience retail and leisure. The business selects assets and tenants, manages leases and reallocates capital through acquisitions and disposals. Revenue depends on rents, occupancy and contractual reviews, while property values reflect both the expected income and market financing conditions. Longer leases can improve visibility but make tenant quality important. Its investment approach focuses on buildings that meet occupiers' operational needs, with borrowing costs and the terms of lease agreements influencing shareholder returns.",
